Finding: {"title":"Process-local in-memory state (customerCache, recentErrors, lastSyncTime) is unsafe on serverless/multi-instance deployment","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"business-rules / correctness","files":["src/lib/quickbooks-sync.ts"],"detail":"`customerCache` (line 88), `lastSyncTime` (line 92), and `recentErrors` (lines 93-98) are module-level variables holding process-local state, used by `findOrCreateQBCustomer`, `syncInvoiceToQuickBooks`, `syncPaymentToQuickBooks`, and surfaced via `getSyncStatus()` (used by `/quickbooks/sync/status`).","impact":"On Vercel/serverless, each invocation may run in a different or freshly cold-started context, so `customerCache` provides no reliable cross-request benefit and can serve a stale QB customer ID after a customer merge/dedup in QBO. `lastSyncTime`/`recentErrors` reported by the sync dashboard are inconsistent per-instance and lose all history on cold start — exactly what the newer `qb_sync_log` table with its `/quickbooks/diagnostics` endpoint was built to replace.","recommendation":"If `quickbooks-sync.ts` remains active, replace `customerCache` with a persisted lookup (e.g. `qb_entity_map` keyed by `atosEntityType='customer'`) and replace `recentErrors`/`lastSyncTime` with a query against `qb_sync_log`.","confidence":"MEDIUM"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

